1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,215
M: Deanna, you picked up the order from the grocery store, right?

2
00:00:03,535 --> 00:00:04,075
W: That's correct.

3
00:00:04,795 --> 00:00:07,275
I went in the morning before I showed up for work.

4
00:00:07,895 --> 00:00:08,830
Is there a problem?

5
00:00:09,405 --> 00:00:11,615
M: Yeah, it looks like we didn't get enough flour.

6
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:14,595
There were only ten kilograms in the box.

7
00:00:15,415 --> 00:00:19,095
That's not enough to bake all the cakes and cookies which our customers ordered today.

8
00:00:20,035 --> 00:00:21,780
W: Keith told me that was how much we needed.

9
00:00:22,155 --> 00:00:23,235
I guess he made a mistake.

10
00:00:24,675 --> 00:00:26,590
M: Actually, we need double that amount.

11
00:00:27,195 --> 00:00:29,270
Would you mind going back and purchasing some more?

12
00:00:29,895 --> 00:00:32,240
Be sure to get a receipt so I can pay you back.

13
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:32,995
W: All right.

14
00:00:33,335 --> 00:00:34,775
I should return in half an hour.
